 const lab:CatalogLab={id:'lab-'+(globalThis.crypto?.randomUUID?.()??Date.now().toString(36)+'-'+Math.random().toString(36).slice(2)),catalogId:'single-area-ospfv2',name:'Single-Area OSPFv2'+(mode==='completed'?' · Completed':''),devices,links:[link('r1-r2',r1,g(1),r2,g(1)),link('r2-r3',r2,g(2),r3,g(1)),link('direct',r1,g(2),r3,g(2)),...hosts.map((h,i)=>link('lan'+(i+1),routers[i],g(0),h,'GigabitEthernet0'))],notes:[{id:'note-ospfv2',x:960,y:600,text:'OSPFv2 · Area 0\nPassive LANs · P2P transits\nR1 ↔ R3 cost 5 · other transits cost 10'}],lesson:{title:'Single-Area OSPFv2',description:'All interfaces and host gateways are addressed, but no static routes or routing protocols are configured. Build one OSPFv2 Area 0 across R1, R2 and R3. The hosts use IPv4 only.\n\nConfigure process 10 and unique router IDs: R1 1.1.1.1, R2 2.2.2.2, R3 3.3.3.3. Add each local LAN and both transit subnets with network statements and the correct wildcard masks. A network statement enables OSPF on matching local interfaces; it is not a remote static route. The process ID is local to each router, while area IDs must agree on each link.\n\nUse passive-interface default, then no passive-interface for Gi0/1 and Gi0/2. Each Gi0/0 LAN stays passive but its connected /24 is advertised. Set both ends of every router transit to point-to-point. These links should show FULL/- without a DR/BDR election. Configure cost 10 on the R1–R2 and R2–R3 transits and cost 5 on both ends of R1–R3. Default Hello/Dead timers remain 10/40 seconds.\n\nWait for two Full neighbors on each router and inspect the Area 0 database. Learn both remote LANs as intra-area O routes at AD 110. R1 to the server LAN should use the direct Gi0/2 link with metric 6: cost 5 plus the destination LAN cost 1. Run all four traffic checks and compare actual traceroute with the selected next hop.\n\nShut R1 Gi0/2 and allow adjacency withdrawal, LSA flooding and SPF. R1 and R3 should reroute through R2 at cost 21. Repeat PC1/server traffic in both directions and inspect both route tables. Restore the interface, wait for Full adjacency, and verify the direct cost-6 path returns. The live configuration, adjacency and route tasks require the complete restored topology before finishing.\n\nFor troubleshooting, make one transit passive or change only its area. Its neighbor must disappear even if the alternate path still carries traffic. Remove the server LAN network statement to observe loss of the learned route while transit adjacencies remain Full, then restore it. Keep the host-facing LANs passive and avoid static routes or default routes that would hide an OSPF fault. Save all three routers with write memory and save or export the lab.',objectives:[
  ...routers.map((d,i)=>({id:'r'+(i+1)+'-area0',title:`Enable R${i+1}’s LAN and both transits in Area 0`,description:`OSPF process 10, router ID ${i+1}.${i+1}.${i+1}.${i+1}; match the three local subnets.`,criterion:{kind:'all' as const,criteria:[0,1,2].map(n=>ospf(d,n,{processId:10,routerId:`${i+1}.${i+1}.${i+1}.${i+1}`,area:0}))}})),
  {id:'interface-policy',title:'Keep LANs passive and configure transit network types and costs',description:'Gi0/0 passive on every router. Gi0/1–2 active and point-to-point; direct R1/R3 cost 5, all other transit ends cost 10.',criterion:{kind:'all',criteria:routers.flatMap(d=>[ospf(d,0,{passive:true}),...[1,2].map(n=>ospf(d,n,{passive:false,networkType:'point-to-point',configuredCost:n===2&&d!==r2?5:10}))])}},
  {id:'full-neighbors',title:'Verify all six directed neighbor relationships are Full',description:'Each router must receive Hello and database-exchange packets from both of its intended peers.',criterion:{kind:'all',criteria:[neighbor(r1,r2,1),neighbor(r2,r1,1),neighbor(r2,r3,2),neighbor(r3,r2,1),neighbor(r1,r3,2),neighbor(r3,r1,2)]}},
  {id:'learned-lans',title:'Verify intra-area O routes to both remote LANs on each router',description:'AD 110; R1/R3 direct LAN routes have metric 6, and the other remote LAN routes have metric 11.',criterion:{kind:'all',criteria:[route(r1,'192.168.20.0','10.0.12.2',1),route(r1,'192.168.30.0','10.0.13.2',2),route(r2,'192.168.10.0','10.0.12.1',1),route(r2,'192.168.30.0','10.0.23.2',2),route(r3,'192.168.10.0','10.0.13.1',2),route(r3,'192.168.20.0','10.0.23.1',1)]}},
  ping('pc1-pc2','Verify PC1 reaches PC2',pc1,'192.168.20.10','Checks learned LAN routes and the return path through R2.'),
  ping('pc1-server','Verify PC1 reaches SRV1',pc1,'192.168.30.10','Repeat during direct-link failure and after recovery.'),
  ping('server-pc1','Verify SRV1 reaches PC1',server,'192.168.10.10','Checks return routing in normal and alternate-path operation.'),
  ping('pc2-server','Verify PC2 reaches SRV1',pc2,'192.168.30.10','Checks the R2/R3 adjacency and both LAN advertisements.'),
 ]}};
